Z||000004||theogre||01-11-2001||08:11 PM||||check all the ground ties on the block. Those can screw up the tach if they are loose or damaged.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ronnie||01-11-2001||08:18 PM||||My tach is messed up also.It idles at about 2000 rpm and as soon as you get going , it jumps all the way to 5-6000. Been thinking about getting another tach filter, but wasn't sure if that would fix it or not.||||reg||6
Z||000006||beachbomb||01-12-2001||02:34 PM||||My tach was all screwed up for a while too, i thought it was the tach filter, replaced that but didn't help, i finally replace the whole gauge cluster(including the tach), worked perfect! Try the tach filter first, alot easier!!!..Jim(2 '84 Indys)||||reg||1
